        "id": "ch17_7_3-1",
        "text": "Conditions\nConditions are accomplished via if statements; they will check the Boolean\nresults of a condition to evaluate the condition. If the return result is True , then\nthe condition will be met, and if it\u2019s False , the condition will not execute. The\ndefinition may look fancy, but the principle is straightforward when you start\npracticing. Here\u2019s an example:\ndef login (password):\nif (password == \"MrRobot\"):\nprint (\"Welcome to FSociety!\")\nsecret = input (\"Enter your password: \")\n#call the login function\nlogin(secret)\nHere\u2019s how it looks in the output window:\nEnter your password: MrRobot\nWelcome to FSociety!\nEsta secci\u00f3n contiene las siguientes subsecciones\n\u2022 if/else Statement\nSi deseas explorar cualquiera de estas subsecciones, puedes pregunt\u00e1rmelo directamente.",
